For 45 Mins DSA

Phase 1: Clarify & Define Bounds : 5M (0–5 )
            Goal
                Think like a Tech Lead before coding
            Clarify constraints
                input size, memory limits, negatives, duplicates, overflow risks.
            Understand system context
                streaming vs batch, read-heavy vs write-heavy.
            State assumptions clearly 
                (e.g., “Assuming input fits in memory initially.”)

Phase 2: Architecture & Complexity Pitch : 7M (5–12)
            Goal
              Align on the solution strategy early
            Mention brute force briefly with exact complexity and why it fails at scale.
            Present the optimal approach and the core pattern/data structure.
            Explain the complexity improvement clearly.
            Pause and confirm alignment before coding.

Phase 3: Modular Implementation : 18M (12–30)
            Goal
              Write production-quality code
            Think out loud continuously — explain decisions and tradeoffs.
            Keep logic modular
              stub helper functions if needed.
            Prefer iterative approaches over deep recursion when possible.
            Use clean naming and defensive edge-case handling

Phase 4: Dry Run & Edge Validation :5M (30–35)
            Goal
              Validate correctness without relying on the compiler
            Walk through a concrete example step-by-step.
            Test edge cases explicitly: empty input, single element, overflow, negatives.
            If you find a bug, fix it calmly and explain the reasoning

Phase 5: Senior-Level Follow-ups: 7M (35–42)
            Goal
              Show architectural depth under changing constraints.
            Expect follow-ups around 
              concurrency, scaling, or distributed systems.
            Discuss tradeoffs 
              using system design concepts like thread safety, locks, partitioning, caching, and memory optimization.
            Focus on architecture even if full implementation isn’t feasible

Phase 6: Reverse Interview : 3M (42–45 min) 
